    sha256: bcaea58ee40a9dca60a21b0f79c525a1f15e95c6b8315d6aaa73f0f53dd5460f
  body: "# Gross income other than earnings for JSA(IB) and IS\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nFor income
    other than earnings, the captured chapter starts with a gross amount and identifies specified sums
    and disregards to consider, rather than permitting all expenses or deductions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\
    \nDMG 28003 has a JSA/IS 64 memo call-out. This passage does not settle every payment category, recovery
    deduction, tax adjustment or disregard. The JSA(Cont) pension-payment exception and separate employed-earnings
    net calculation must not be conflated with this treatment.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG
    28003, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28000, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review
    is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring
    time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document,
    individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter
    reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural
    evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch26`: PDF SHA-256 `fe619693d2f8cc78cac3786dadab88e81467ec56d38f00727285612af92b80c9`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `f4089f7088e6a987d028072f4968eb39f2686b7a588e2c38f8ebc1cb3042102a`.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch28`:
    PDF SHA-256 `bcaea58ee40a9dca60a21b0f79c525a1f15e95c6b8315d6aaa73f0f53dd5460f`; extracted pages SHA-256
    `f7e554c1af4c7d8b915524f441c1680c5bea7429ac8fff9fd18bc0c925f25c31`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-net-employed-earnings
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The passages provide distinct treatments for other income and employed earnings; the
      association records this boundary and does not equate their deductions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch28/0003
      quote: "28003 [See DMG Memo IS/JSA 64] The DM should take into account the gross amount of any income
        1.\nReferences in this Chapter to income means income other than earnings. When calculating gross
        income\ndisregard the sums in DMG 28008 - 28010 and DMG 28150 et seq. No disregards should be
        made for\nany other expenses or deductions.\n\n\n                                            \
        \               1 JSA Regs, reg 103(1); IS (Gen) Regs, reg 40(1)"
      locator: DMG 28003
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch26/0009
      quote: "26020 Net earnings are gross earnings less1\n\n\n1. income tax and\n\n\n2. Class 1 SS contributions
        and\n\n\n3. half of any sum paid by the employee, towards an occupational or personal pension
        scheme.\n\n\n                                                          1 JSA Regs, reg 99(4);
        IS (Gen) Regs, reg 36(3)"
      locator: DMG 26020
